  "term": "cytogenetic map",
  "definition": "A cytogenetic map is the microscope-visible banding pattern of a stained chromosome. The light and dark bands give each chromosome a distinctive look, which helps clinicians study chromosomes in a karyotype and detect chromosomal changes.",
